WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.400
Lab 2 reads a real test project.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.672
You need a Google Cloud test
project, never production,

3
00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.725
its project owner, and a
Google group for the reader.

4
00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:13.863
Enable the A P I, grant the viewer
role, and sign in as the reader.

5
00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:17.126
Then cross-check Google's own
command against the collection.

6
00:00:17.126 --> 00:00:21.087
The project may have no incidents
at all, and that's a valid result.

7
00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:25.962
Then the part that makes this gate
different: record the gaps with the ISSO.

8
00:00:25.962 --> 00:00:30.787
Whether the project is in an Assured
Workloads FedRAMP or I L package, and in

9
00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:35.612
every case, that Google's planned
maintenance doesn't come through this A P I.

10
00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:40.149
To back it out, step four removes
the role binding and deletes the run.

11
00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:45.038
It leaves the A P I enabled, unless
the project owner decides otherwise.

12
00:00:45.038 --> 00:00:47.188
The authors haven't run Lab 2.

13
00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:50.420
The workbook's Chapter 5
has the exact commands.
